Subject: [PATCH 07195/11362] [outer-loop] REQ-ARC-FCP-5699-14: close 5699-13
 gap -- exploration exhaustion ruled out, new plan-finding lead found

Extended scripts/arc_sge_live_path_ab.py to capture policy.explorer.explored_out
and policy.induction_attempts for both arms, re-ran on sp80 (budget=250, matching
REQ-ARC-FCP-5699-12's config for direct comparability).

Finding 1 (closes 5699-13's open gap): explorer_explored_out=False for both arms --
the real ~48-candidate rich_action_candidates() generator does not hit the smoke
test's frontier-exhaustion wall. 5699-7/8/9/10's exhaustion framing is confirmed to
be an artifact of the smoke-test harness's narrow 8-candidate generator, not a
property of the real live-agent stack.

Finding 2 (new lead): induction fires exactly once per arm as designed
(reason=stall at transition_count=25). The single attempt threads through two
tiers, both declining to plan for different reasons: tier 1 (CNN-dynamics-prior
warm-start, gated_engine_from_transitions) PASSES its own held-out trust gate
(heldout_cell_recall 0.98-1.0) yet e3.plan_in_model finds no plan against the
trusted engine; tier 2 (DSL/LLM engine, WorldModelVerifier-gated) fails on both
verify_accuracy and verify_cell_recall, so the CARNOT_ARC_TRUST_METRIC=cell_recall
escape hatch would not have rescued this attempt either. n=1 game/attempt --
documented as a lead, not a generalized claim, per Sample-Size Rigor discipline.

